# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default Frappe apps offered by ./setup.sh
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One app per line:   name|repository|depends|features|description
#
#   name         Frappe app name (the folder in frappe-bench/apps). The .env key
#                holding its version is the upper-cased name + _VERSION.
#   repository   git URL used for `bench get-app` and for listing tags.
#   depends      comma-separated apps that must also be installed (setup.sh
#                selects them automatically; they are installed first).
#   features     comma-separated flags understood by the scripts:
#                  follows-frappe  version numbers track Frappe's major version
#                                  (the picker shows matching tags first)
#                  sfu             needs the Meet SFU: adds the meet-sfu
#                                  container and the JWT/announced-IP settings
#   description  shown in the setup.sh menu.
#
# The order of this file is the install order (dependencies are always moved
# before the apps that need them). The "frappe" line is mandatory: it is the
# framework itself and is always installed.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
frappe|https://github.com/frappe/frappe|||Frappe Framework (always installed)
erpnext|https://github.com/frappe/erpnext||follows-frappe|ERP: accounting, stock, selling, buying, manufacturing
hrms|https://github.com/frappe/hrms|erpnext|follows-frappe|HR and payroll
raven|https://github.com/frappe/raven|||Team chat
meet|https://github.com/frappe/meet||sfu|Video meetings (adds the meet-sfu container)
drive|https://github.com/frappe/drive|||File storage and sharing
insights|https://github.com/frappe/insights|||Business intelligence and dashboards
wiki|https://github.com/frappe/wiki|||Knowledge base
